      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Economists generally argue that international trade agreements and institutions like the WTO reduce barriers to exchange, which allows countries to specialize in goods where they have a comparative advantage. This specialization boosts global productivity and GDP while offering consumers a wider variety of cheaper goods and services. Furthermore, these frameworks stabilize markets by providing a democratic venue to resolve disputes, preventing the trade wars that often lead to economic instability. Ultimately, by lowering costs and fostering mutual benefits across borders, these agreements create a more efficient and prosperous global economy for all participating nations.",
